                <div class="webinar-grid--content--description">
                    <p>Electrolyser development and deployment is progressing, but the conversation is shifting. It is no longer just about scale, attention is now turning to selection and choosing the right technology for the right application.</p>
<p>Alkaline, PEM, SOEC and emerging variants each bring distinct advantages and trade-offs. From efficiency and durability, to investment considerations and integration with renewable power, technology choice is increasingly defining project performance and viability.</p>
<p>If projects are to move towards a final investment decision, developers, investors and end users must balance technical capability with commercial reality. Grid connection, operating profiles, purity requirements and downstream use cases are all shaping a more nuanced decision-making process around electrolyser selection.</p>
<p>In this exclusive H2 View webinar, we will look at how different electrolysers compare, where each makes sense, and what stakeholders should consider before committing.</p>
<p>Join hosts Thomas Dee and Rob Cockerill, alongside a panel of industry experts, as we break down the practical, technical and commercial factors shaping electrolyser selection strategy – and answer your questions.</p>
